unlock.gif?t=1744639160\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">forge a personalised, eldritch cue from parts collected along the way</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">test your sanity and fight void-born bosses on different tables</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">unlock new loot: powerups, balls, cue parts and more</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2873750/extras/header_03_small.png?t=1744639160\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Pool of Madness does not hold your hand, <strong>respects mystery and encourages experimentation</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2873750/extras/fish_finish.gif?t=1744639160\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Taking inspiration from all across the spectrum, from traditional roguelikes like Brogue, to genre-defining titles like Dark Souls and Inscryption... and - well - pool, it emphasises discovery and replayability, inviting you to break the rules and <strong>develop your own unusual strategies</strong> in order to survive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2873750/extras/lewitacjagif_30fps.gif?t=1744639160\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">no hand holding, only the void</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">endless replayability</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">freedom to experiment and break the rules</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><